WEBVTT

00:04.000 --> 00:06.227
Hey guys, can I share
something with you?

00:06.229 --> 00:07.558
Sure.
Yeah. Go ahead.

00:07.560 --> 00:11.149
Well, you know how I don't ever
brag about my sexual exploits.

00:11.151 --> 00:12.878
That would be an
accurate statement, yes.

00:12.880 --> 00:16.271
Well, last night,
bonnie and I got really kinky.

00:16.273 --> 00:17.467
She painted my toenails.

00:17.469 --> 00:18.331
(giggles)

00:18.333 --> 00:20.262
Wha...?
You serious?

00:20.264 --> 00:22.190
Check it out.

00:23.920 --> 00:25.449
What the hell is that?!

00:25.451 --> 00:26.514
Nail polish.

00:26.516 --> 00:27.610
No. The foot.

00:27.612 --> 00:30.238
It's a child's foot, joe.

00:30.240 --> 00:32.398
Wha... I-I don't... You-you were
crippled when you were an adult.

00:32.400 --> 00:33.496
How the hell did...?
Yeah.

00:33.498 --> 00:35.260
A few months back,
I got really drunk

00:35.262 --> 00:37.420
And was playing around
with an elastic band.

00:37.422 --> 00:40.215
I wrapped it around my thigh
and forgot about it

00:40.217 --> 00:43.107
For a week or two and uh, yeah,
so, that's my left foot now.

00:43.109 --> 00:44.204
(sighs)

00:44.206 --> 00:45.734
I mean,
it still works the same.

00:45.735 --> 00:46.865
Oh, yeah, sure.

00:46.867 --> 00:48.427
Still a foot, I guess.

00:48.429 --> 00:49.757
Cleveland:
Whassup?

00:49.759 --> 00:51.022
<i>( the cleveland show theme
stinger plays)</i>

00:51.024 --> 00:52.418
Oh, hey, cleveland.
Hi.

00:52.420 --> 00:53.948
Wait, don't you have
a show to do?

00:53.950 --> 00:55.875
(laughs):
Oh... That's right.

00:55.877 --> 00:58.039
All right.
I knew this was coming.

00:58.041 --> 00:59.700
Everybody give me
your best shot.

00:59.702 --> 01:01.230
Oh, my god.
Where do I even begin?

01:01.232 --> 01:03.026
You know,
it's not a good sign

01:03.028 --> 01:03.925
That this is
the first time

01:03.927 --> 01:04.988
A lot of people
are realizing

01:04.990 --> 01:06.019
<i>You had a show.</i>

01:06.021 --> 01:07.315
Your logo was stupid.

01:07.317 --> 01:08.812
It looked like
a big, purple penis

01:08.814 --> 01:09.876
And your ratings blew.

01:09.878 --> 01:12.704
<i>We did about the same
as bob's burgers.</i>

01:12.706 --> 01:13.801
That's your bar!?

01:13.803 --> 01:15.032
Oh, shame on you!

01:15.034 --> 01:17.059
This is good.
This is constructive.

01:17.061 --> 01:18.889
The talking bear
was so bad,

01:18.891 --> 01:21.349
Seth macfarlane quit voicing him
after season two.

01:21.351 --> 01:23.644
It's hard to make
a talking bear funny.

01:23.646 --> 01:26.471
(laughing): It worked out
okay in movie form.

01:26.473 --> 01:28.500
What was supposed to be
the show's audience?

01:28.502 --> 01:29.496
Who did you make it for?

01:29.498 --> 01:30.594
Like, some black guy

01:30.596 --> 01:32.156
Who's never met
another black guy?

01:32.158 --> 01:33.920
Anything else?
Yeah.

01:33.922 --> 01:36.946
Here's four seasons worth of
dvds of what we've been up to.

01:36.948 --> 01:38.675
You know, just so you're
back up the speed.

01:38.677 --> 01:42.133
And I'll warn you ahead of time:
These have jokes in them.

01:42.135 --> 01:43.963
I...

01:43.965 --> 01:46.424
I don't have
a dvd player.

01:46.426 --> 01:50.381
¶ it seems today
that all you see ¶

01:50.383 --> 01:53.573
¶ is violence in movies
and sex on tv ¶

01:53.575 --> 01:56.865
¶ but where are those
good old-fashioned values ¶

01:56.867 --> 01:59.792
¶ on which we used to rely? ¶

01:59.794 --> 02:03.849
¶ lucky there's a family guy ¶

02:03.851 --> 02:06.874
¶ lucky there's a man
who positively can do ¶

02:06.876 --> 02:08.704
¶ all the things
that make us... ¶

02:08.706 --> 02:11.764
Excuse me.
Excuse me. Sorry.

02:11.766 --> 02:13.859
Sorry, mort.
I-I hate to do this.

02:13.861 --> 02:15.687
What... What's happening?

02:15.689 --> 02:16.884
They want me in the line.

02:16.886 --> 02:18.315
Well, where do I go?

02:18.317 --> 02:19.578
Home?

02:19.580 --> 02:21.672
Okay, but I still
get paid for today, right?

02:21.674 --> 02:23.337
I... I wouldn't know.

02:23.339 --> 02:25.033
You need to talk to marla.

02:27.695 --> 02:29.222
Sorry.
(mort grunts)

02:29.224 --> 02:30.154
You okay?

02:30.156 --> 02:31.550
What do you care?

02:33.979 --> 02:35.807
¶ all the things that make us ¶

02:35.809 --> 02:37.604
¶ laugh and cry ¶

02:37.606 --> 02:42.757
¶ he's... A...
Fam... Ily... Guy! ¶

02:49.575 --> 02:51.104
It'll be nice
having cleveland

02:51.106 --> 02:52.302
Back across
the street.

02:52.304 --> 02:53.565
Why?

02:53.567 --> 02:55.627
I think a lot of times
you only say things

02:55.629 --> 02:56.890
Because they make
you sound good.

02:56.892 --> 02:58.554
You know, cleveland,
it must be weird

02:58.556 --> 03:01.147
For you guys to move and
not 'cause of a hurricane.

03:01.149 --> 03:03.574
Oh, lois, I'm so
glad to see

03:03.576 --> 03:05.703
Peter and cleveland
back together again.

03:05.705 --> 03:06.966
Yeah, me too.

03:06.968 --> 03:08.562
Now peter will have
something to do

03:08.564 --> 03:09.559
Besides flushing
the toilet

03:09.561 --> 03:11.257
To foghat's
"slow ride."

03:11.259 --> 03:13.451
("slow ride" begins)
peter, what are you
doing in there?

03:13.453 --> 03:14.616
Peter:
Nothin'.

03:14.618 --> 03:15.912
¶ slow ride ¶

03:15.914 --> 03:18.272
(toilet flushes)

03:18.274 --> 03:20.202
¶ take it easy ¶

03:20.204 --> 03:22.431
(toilet flushes)

03:22.433 --> 03:23.927
¶ slow ride ¶

03:23.929 --> 03:25.688
(toilet handle rattling)

03:25.690 --> 03:27.883
Peter, you're wasting
tons of water!

03:27.885 --> 03:29.047
Peter:
It's not a waste!

03:29.049 --> 03:30.810
And we need a faster toilet.

03:30.812 --> 03:32.239
'sup, man?

03:32.241 --> 03:33.404
Yeah, yeah, "sup."

03:33.406 --> 03:35.466
<i>Keep walkin', you
boondocks rip-off.</i>

03:37.064 --> 03:38.725
Home, sweet...

03:38.727 --> 03:39.856
Huh?!

03:42.484 --> 03:44.777
This house is a
disastrous area!

03:44.779 --> 03:46.706
I can't move my
family in here.

03:46.708 --> 03:47.836
You're right.

03:47.838 --> 03:49.432
Well, we'll all have
to do our part.

03:49.434 --> 03:51.195
I'll take little
cocoa butter here.

03:51.197 --> 03:52.427
(laughs)

03:52.429 --> 03:53.756
What the hell
happened?

03:53.758 --> 03:55.418
Well, a lot of people
rented your house.

03:55.420 --> 03:57.015
Uh, ryan reynolds,

03:57.017 --> 03:58.445
Chevy chase
and dan aykroyd...

03:58.447 --> 04:00.108
For a while, it
was an orphanage

04:00.110 --> 04:02.469
Where the children
sang desolate songs.

04:02.471 --> 04:07.124
¶ we're too old
to ever be adopted ¶

04:07.126 --> 04:12.811
¶ no one wants
a nine-year-old. ¶

04:12.813 --> 04:15.471
Peter: Shut up,
you bastards!

04:18.565 --> 04:20.924
I really appreciate y'all

04:20.926 --> 04:22.555
Helpin' me fix up my house.

04:22.557 --> 04:23.553
Yeah, no problem,
cleveland.

04:23.555 --> 04:24.750
Hey, where do you
want me to put

04:24.752 --> 04:26.179
All these giraffe
figurines?

04:26.181 --> 04:27.210
Just spread 'em out.

04:27.212 --> 04:29.538
Don't make any one
room too giraffey.

04:29.540 --> 04:31.366
Cleveland, where should
I hang the mirror?

04:31.368 --> 04:32.431
Right about here?

04:32.433 --> 04:33.927
Maybe a
little higher.

04:33.929 --> 04:35.358
Oh, like, uh,
up here?

04:35.360 --> 04:37.021
I think
maybe higher.

04:37.023 --> 04:38.683
You don't want
it too high, now.

04:38.685 --> 04:40.744
Let's get you a
different job, joe.

04:40.746 --> 04:42.042
Are you sure?

04:42.044 --> 04:44.202
'cause I already hung
all these paintings.

04:44.204 --> 04:47.230
This place is shaping up
real nice.

04:50.190 --> 04:52.018
Hey, cleveland,
what's that?

04:52.020 --> 04:53.813
Oh, this is
my bead door.

04:53.815 --> 04:54.879
It looks stupid.

04:54.881 --> 04:56.607
Why don't you walk
through it?

04:59.934 --> 05:01.163
How do you feel?

05:01.165 --> 05:02.460
Awesome!

05:02.462 --> 05:04.754
Like a suitcase
comin' out of the airport.

05:04.756 --> 05:06.251
Yeah, or
like a bug

05:06.253 --> 05:08.711
Walkin' through
stevie wonder's hair.

05:12.903 --> 05:16.093
Turns out this old house is
lacking in storage space,

05:16.095 --> 05:18.089
So I gotta make some
tough decisions.

05:18.091 --> 05:19.654
You gonna keep
these neckties?

05:19.656 --> 05:21.049
Yeah, throw 'em
in my car.

05:21.051 --> 05:22.579
They're just to keep
my trunk closed

05:22.581 --> 05:24.276
What if I'm ever
haulin' garbage.

05:24.278 --> 05:25.473
I ain't no lawyer.

05:25.475 --> 05:27.368
I use whatever
for my purposes.

05:27.370 --> 05:28.930
Could be a box spring.

05:28.932 --> 05:30.194
Could be a
old radio.

05:30.196 --> 05:32.123
Could be a more
recent radio...

05:32.125 --> 05:33.087
Wait, now
I'm confused.

05:33.089 --> 05:35.116
So... So some of this
stuff isn't trash?

05:35.118 --> 05:36.578
Like this
old computer monitor?

05:36.580 --> 05:38.010
Nah, that's a
sittin' chair,

05:38.012 --> 05:39.006
What for children.

05:39.008 --> 05:40.603
How about this telephone cord?

05:40.605 --> 05:42.033
That's a pet leash.

05:42.035 --> 05:44.395
If the good lord decideth
we should have one.

05:44.397 --> 05:46.057
I'm gonna go
ahead and ditch

05:46.059 --> 05:48.185
These promotional
mcdonald's cups
from the 80's.

05:48.187 --> 05:49.881
Nah, that's all
we drink from.

05:49.883 --> 05:51.344
That's the riddler
right there.

05:51.346 --> 05:54.304
He would make inquiries
to set your mind a-jumble.

05:54.306 --> 05:56.732
How do you live in a
house with all this junk?

05:56.734 --> 05:58.693
I'd rather stay in a
house with small kids.

05:58.695 --> 06:01.054
So you can sleep
on the couch.

06:01.056 --> 06:03.017
Uh, please take
the potty seat
off the toilet,

06:03.019 --> 06:04.182
Don't try to
pee through it.

06:04.184 --> 06:06.042
There's juice boxes
in the fridge

06:06.044 --> 06:08.370
And if you get hungry,
there's plenty of
goldfish in the couch.

06:08.372 --> 06:11.363
Um, feel free to watch
tv with the sound off.

06:11.365 --> 06:12.959
And the kids
will be down here

06:12.961 --> 06:15.654
First thing in the morning
to antagonize the dogs.

06:15.656 --> 06:17.715
Oh, and everyone
here has pinkeye.

06:22.772 --> 06:25.664
"...And that was the moment
I stopped being dwayne johnson

06:25.666 --> 06:27.891
And started being the rock."

06:27.893 --> 06:29.786
That's a good place
to leave off.

06:29.788 --> 06:31.149
Hey, I just realized.

06:31.151 --> 06:32.147
We're the rock!

06:32.149 --> 06:33.211
What do you mean?

06:33.213 --> 06:34.609
Together, you and I

06:34.611 --> 06:36.871
Make one biracial
wrestler.

06:36.873 --> 06:38.765
(gasps) do you have any
folding chairs?

06:38.767 --> 06:39.930
No.

06:39.932 --> 06:40.959
That's all right.
I'll use this.

06:40.961 --> 06:42.091
Folding chair!

06:42.093 --> 06:43.089
Ow!

06:43.091 --> 06:44.186
Donna:
What was that?!

06:44.188 --> 06:45.350
(gasps)

06:45.352 --> 06:47.046
That was my
great-grandma's vase!

06:47.048 --> 06:48.741
On the drive up
from virginia,

06:48.743 --> 06:50.670
She kept that vase
'tween her legs.

06:51.769 --> 06:52.932
W-what are you doing?!

06:52.934 --> 06:55.160
Making sure you
learn your lesson.

06:55.162 --> 06:56.823
Ow! It hurts!

06:56.825 --> 06:58.054
It hurts!

06:58.056 --> 07:00.049
I can't believe japanese men

07:00.051 --> 07:01.712
Pay good money for this.

07:01.714 --> 07:04.704
At work, I am
important businessman.

07:04.706 --> 07:08.261
Here, I am bad boy!

07:13.783 --> 07:15.212
Tv announcer:
We now return to

07:15.214 --> 07:16.775
<i>The gay bachelor.</i>

07:16.777 --> 07:18.670
Ew, they're
all gross!

07:18.672 --> 07:20.267
I'm keeping
the roses.

07:20.269 --> 07:22.794
Mom!
Mrs. Brown spanked me!

07:22.796 --> 07:23.959
What?!

07:23.961 --> 07:26.320
And you still haven't
pulled up your pants?

07:26.322 --> 07:27.483
Chris, what
happened?

07:27.485 --> 07:29.645
I was playing with rallo
and I broke a vase

07:29.647 --> 07:31.773
And then she gave me
a spanking!

07:31.775 --> 07:34.400
Uh, I believe the term
is "whuppin'", chris.

07:34.402 --> 07:36.064
God, look at the size
of that handprint.

07:36.066 --> 07:37.726
It's like doctor j.

07:37.728 --> 07:38.990
Peter, this
is serious!

07:38.992 --> 07:40.651
A woman hit
our child!

07:40.653 --> 07:42.249
What is wrong
with her?

07:42.251 --> 07:44.609
Whoa, can I get
some white bread

07:44.611 --> 07:45.806
On that judgmental
sandwich?

07:45.808 --> 07:47.702
Brian, why are you
bringing race into this?

07:47.704 --> 07:49.266
Lois, I've
spent my life

07:49.268 --> 07:51.127
Trying to keep
race out of things.

07:51.129 --> 07:52.790
That's why whenever
I walk into lids,

07:52.792 --> 07:54.220
Every guy
fist-bumps me.

07:54.222 --> 07:55.849
Oh, you're
full of crap, brian.

07:55.851 --> 07:57.679
I'm just saying,
lois, some of us

07:57.681 --> 07:59.209
Go through life
without seeing color.

07:59.211 --> 08:01.238
That's because you're
color blind, brian.

08:01.240 --> 08:02.235
You're right.

08:02.237 --> 08:03.531
I am color blind.

08:03.533 --> 08:04.695
Here...

08:04.697 --> 08:05.925
And here.

08:05.927 --> 08:08.020
Hey, remember when you
swallowed that rib-eye bone

08:08.022 --> 08:09.352
And you couldn't
poop it out?

08:09.354 --> 08:10.482
And then you
pushed real hard

08:10.484 --> 08:12.543
And the poo came through
the rib eye hole?

08:12.545 --> 08:15.204
Peter, we gotta go
over there and
talk to donna.

08:15.206 --> 08:17.298
All right, but you need
to cool down first, lois.

08:17.300 --> 08:18.629
Find a way
to channel your anger.

08:18.631 --> 08:21.023
What I do is throw
a shot put into a crowd

08:21.025 --> 08:22.620
And make it look
like an accident.

08:25.447 --> 08:26.678
(grunts)

08:26.680 --> 08:29.038
I forgot to make it
look like an accident.

08:32.099 --> 08:33.595
(doorbell ringing)

08:33.597 --> 08:35.323
That woman
is gonna be sorry

08:35.325 --> 08:36.852
She laid her hands
on our son.

08:36.854 --> 08:38.583
Hello.

08:38.585 --> 08:39.613
Hi, j-just
so you know,

08:39.614 --> 08:40.909
This is sort of
lois's thing.

08:40.911 --> 08:42.472
I-I'm not really
upset about it.

08:42.474 --> 08:43.469
So... Go
ahead, dear.

08:43.471 --> 08:44.634
Donna, what gives you

08:44.636 --> 08:46.132
The right to
spank my child?

08:46.134 --> 08:48.326
It always smells like
the same meal over here.

08:48.328 --> 08:49.921
I hit him
for a reason.

08:49.923 --> 08:51.420
He broke my vase.

08:51.422 --> 08:53.446
And maybe I wouldn't have
to discipline your child

08:53.448 --> 08:55.143
If you did
it yourself!

08:55.145 --> 08:56.307
Oh, please!

08:56.309 --> 08:57.870
The only thing kids
learn from spanking

08:57.872 --> 09:00.197
Is adults don't have the
patience to teach them.

09:00.199 --> 09:01.396
Bull honkey.

09:01.398 --> 09:02.392
What?!

09:02.394 --> 09:05.185
And my children are
very well-behaved.

09:05.187 --> 09:06.284
Oh, yeah?

09:06.286 --> 09:08.478
Your baby's on
the roof right now.

09:10.508 --> 09:13.066
You get down from there
this instant!

09:13.068 --> 09:14.397
Munch me, bitch!

09:14.399 --> 09:16.493
Right now, stewie,
or you're in time-out!

09:16.495 --> 09:18.188
How many gray pubes
you pluck today,

09:18.190 --> 09:19.185
You old bag?

09:19.187 --> 09:20.847
Your time-outs
are a joke.

09:20.849 --> 09:22.180
You're a
terrible parent.

09:22.182 --> 09:23.710
I'm a terrible
parent?!

09:23.712 --> 09:25.205
You're a child abuser!

09:25.207 --> 09:26.369
You know what?

09:26.371 --> 09:28.165
From now on, I don't
want our families

09:28.167 --> 09:29.827
Having anything to do
with each other!

09:29.829 --> 09:32.021
Well, cleveland, looks like
these two little alley cats

09:32.023 --> 09:33.786
Have scrapped it out.
I'll see you tomorrow.

09:33.788 --> 09:35.115
That includes
you, peter.

09:35.117 --> 09:37.276
I don't want you ever
talking to cleveland again.

09:37.278 --> 09:38.840
And cleveland,
I forbid you

09:38.842 --> 09:41.068
From ever talking
to peter again!

09:48.251 --> 09:49.780
Hey, lois, look!

09:49.782 --> 09:50.977
I'm smoking!

09:50.979 --> 09:52.407
You can't control dick!

09:52.409 --> 09:54.701
I'm a roof baby now!

09:58.661 --> 10:00.388
So we're
making plans

10:00.390 --> 10:02.284
For susie's first
birthday party.

10:02.286 --> 10:03.249
Oh, that's good bar talk.

10:03.251 --> 10:04.378
Hey, y'all..

10:04.380 --> 10:06.242
Oh, oh, uh, sorry,
peter, I'll...

10:06.244 --> 10:07.239
I'll get
outta here.

10:07.241 --> 10:08.237
No, no, no, no,
I'll go.

10:08.239 --> 10:09.235
I'll go.
It's okay.

10:09.237 --> 10:10.364
What's goin' on?

10:10.366 --> 10:12.228
You guys touch
pee-pees or
something?

10:12.230 --> 10:13.226
I wish.

10:13.228 --> 10:15.285
No, our wives
got in a big fight

10:15.287 --> 10:17.215
And banned us from
seeing each other.

10:17.217 --> 10:18.214
So what if they're in a fight?

10:18.216 --> 10:19.743
What does that have
to do with you?

10:19.745 --> 10:21.074
Well, I gotta
live with donna.

10:21.076 --> 10:23.001
Uh-oh.
There she is.

10:24.167 --> 10:25.662
Oh, no!
Peter, quick!

10:25.665 --> 10:27.059
Change pigments!

10:31.150 --> 10:33.044
That was close.

10:33.046 --> 10:35.571
Peter, we can't risk
seeing each other.

10:35.573 --> 10:38.699
But, cleveland, you and I are
pals, and I just got you back.

10:38.701 --> 10:40.526
Well, there might
be one solution.

10:40.528 --> 10:43.620
We just got to hang out where
there's no chance we'll be seen.

10:43.622 --> 10:45.116
You know,
keep it a secret.

10:45.118 --> 10:46.513
Then that's what we'll do.

10:46.515 --> 10:48.176
'cause I can't
lose you again, cleveland.

10:48.178 --> 10:51.301
I'm closer to you than
I am to my own right hand.

10:51.303 --> 10:53.994
Oh, my god,
you like scrambled eggs, too?

10:53.996 --> 10:56.157
Here, go ahead, have some.

10:56.159 --> 10:58.086
Whoa, that's a big bite there.

10:58.088 --> 10:59.316
Slow down, buddy.

10:59.318 --> 11:01.078
(makes choking sounds)

11:01.080 --> 11:03.273
Oh, my god!
Oh, my god! He's choking!

11:03.275 --> 11:05.900
